  "slice_validation": "A separate linked process uses public CPU0 ticks, owner IRQ exit and explicit saved-frame checkpoints to rotate two equal-priority CPU-bound tasks on CPU2 for six slices with no timeout deadlines. It checks immediate local first-peer admission, resume and priority-change rearming, and no slice SGIs for a single task, a preemption-disabled task or an idle owner.",
  "ready_trace_validation": "The selected ready-hook fixture checks the waker CPU, committed notification payload and hook completion before the destination SGI. Repeated notification, owner consumption, timeout followed by late notification, repeated resume and both abort/notification orderings each retain one ready hook per logical wake. Queue and event-group wake hooks retain caller origin. Current-task queries use a nonblocking atomic snapshot.",
  "ready_trace_limits": "The notification ready hook runs immediately after the successful payload transition and before that producer admits a route or publishes an activation/SGI. An independent owner entry can run between payload linearization and the caller hook. Concurrent QEMU trace fidelity remains required before board latency measurements.",
  "api_trace_validation": "Selected entry/return macros count successful and early-return notification/getter paths and global suspend calls. A value-changing notification operation and its previous-value/output checks verify single evaluation; a compile assertion verifies the trace-return value retains BaseType_t. Public routed branches preserve the original entry arguments and emit return hooks after evaluating the declared return value once."
